  "worked_solution": "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed (in feet per second), we divide the number of feet, $280,$ by the number of seconds, $70.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{280}{70}=280\u00f770=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the canoe is $4$ feet per second.",
